<SimplePage lang="en" title="Tickets and refunds">
<p>Most answers are below. If you still need help, <a href="/contact/?topic=tickets">send us a ticket question</a> and we will reply by email.</p>
<h2>Where are my tickets?</h2>
<p>Your tickets are in the confirmation email from the seller you bought from (named on the event page). Check your spam or promotions folder and search for the event name. The seller can resend them.</p>
<h2>Refunds and exchanges</h2>
<p>Refunds are handled by the seller under its terms of sale and the Australian Consumer Law. If an event is cancelled, you are entitled to a refund of the ticket price. If it is rescheduled, your ticket is valid for the new date.</p>
<h2>Changing a name or passing a ticket on</h2>
<p>This depends on the seller. Contact them first; if they can’t help, tell us and we’ll do our best.</p>
<h2>Access needs</h2>
<p>Let us know before the night if you need step-free access, a companion ticket or seating near an exit. See <a href="/help/accessibility/">accessibility</a>.</p>
<h2>Groups and tables</h2>
<p>For group bookings or table packages, <a href="/contact/?topic=tickets">contact us</a> with the event and the number of people.</p>
<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?topic=tickets">Ask a ticket question</a></p>
</SimplePage>
